A||N||5||johnmac||Wheel Bearing - Is it good?||||1||
Z||000000||johnmac||03-26-2001||12:00 AM||||Just pulled my rear wheel bearings on my 120k mileage 'project' 86 Gt.<P>CV joint outside cup was split, some dirt was on the outside of the wheel bearing.<P>No extererior damage can be seen. The bearing turns but does not spin. It turns tight. Is this normal?<P>How does one know if your wheel bearing is good?<P>Were is the best place to buy replacement bearings?<P>Any advise? <P>Thanks,<P>John<P>------------------<BR>John MacHaffie<BR>86GT "Yellowbird"<BR>12+ month project car<BR>johnmac@mpinet.net<BR>Winter Springs, Florida||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||03-26-2001||12:54 AM||||If it's tight and smooth turning, the bearing is good. You will need a new or rebuilt half shaft/or if your handy, tear it down, clean it up, add lube and install a new boot.||||reg||1
Z||000002||862M4inCA||03-26-2001||08:35 AM||||just a side note on this. The rear wheel bearing is actually part of the hub and needs to be replaced as a unit. The bearing itself is not available. Also it would be a good idea to replace both. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||SteveJ||03-26-2001||09:14 AM||||Check out the price of the rebuilt half shaft. They are reasonable. I had trouble when I replaced the boot on a CV tightening the clamp they supply. They use a special tool which I did not have. It came loose and then the joint failed due to dirt getting in.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula88||03-26-2001||01:19 PM||||You can also get split boots as replacements.  Cut off the original, and this one wraps around the joint and is filled with grease.  It'll help get some more mileage out of the CV joint if you caught the bad boot before damage began.  You should be able to find it at most auto parts stores.||||reg||1
Z||000005||prof bobo||03-26-2001||01:43 PM||||I've been using big hose clamps for years with no problems (as long as they don't hit anything -check your clearance).  Put the screw clamps opposite each other on each side of the boots.  No special tool required.||||reg||1
